{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the per-observation likelihood loop `y[n] ~ bernoulli_logit(...)` with a deterministic local linear-predictor vector `eta` followed by one vectorized built-in sampling statement `y ~ bernoulli_logit(eta)`. This preserves the same Bernoulli-logit likelihood while making the protected observation a top-level plain left-hand side, observed exactly once outside loops. Priors and data are unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> J;
  int<lower=1> K;
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> jj;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=K> kk;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> y;
}
parameters {
  real delta;
  array[J] real alpha;
  array[K] real beta;
  array[K] real log_gamma; // log of discrimination of question k
}
model {
  vector[N] eta;

  alpha ~ normal(0, 1);
  beta ~ normal(0, 1);
  delta ~ normal(0.75, 1);
  log_gamma ~ normal(0, 1);

  for (n in 1 : N) {
    eta[n] = exp(log_gamma[kk[n]])
             * (alpha[jj[n]] - beta[kk[n]] + delta);
  }
  y ~ bernoulli_logit(eta);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":4,"K":3,"N":3,"jj":[2,3,2],"kk":[2,1,2],"y":[0,1,0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
